    "isHTML": true,
    "workshopOrigin": "slides",
    "searchText": "Audit opinion and audit report\nWhen is a matter pervasive?\nICAS AA Workshop 4 \n55\nYou are the auditor of Paddington Ltd (Paddington) for the year ended 31 October 20X5. As \npart of the audit of trade receivables you have been reviewing the aged debt analysis to \nensure the reasonableness of Paddington’s allowance for doubtful dents. Trade receivables \nare a significant balance in the accounts, amounting to £26.5m. The directors are insisting on \nan allowance of 5% but you assess that an allowance of £9.8m is necessary. The profit after \nincome taxes (and after deducting the current 5% provision) is £5.5m.\nHow should this matter be treated in the audit report?\n",
    "sourceFiles": [
      "sources/AA WS4 Slides incl Answers.pdf"
    ],
    "linkTags": [
      "aa-module-10"
    ]
