    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/aa-ws4-fairview-slide-e3-q.png\" alt=\"Workshop 4 original source extract\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/aa-ws4-fairview-slide-e3-a.png\" alt=\"Workshop 4 original source extract\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "workshopOrigin": "slides",
    "searchText": "Subsequent events\nEvent 3: Financial Conduct Authority investigation\nThe Financial Conduct Authority (‘FCA’) commenced an investigation of Fairview in October 2X17. The investigation \nstemmed from complaints to the regulatory authorities of ‘overly robust selling techniques’ for loans to a \nspecialised area of the bank’s customers. \nFor the financial year-end 31 March 2X18, a preliminary accrual was made of £2.75 million which represented £1.8 \nmillion for fines and £0.95 million for anticipated compensation costs. \nWith the full cooperation of Fairview staff, the investigation was recently concluded and the FCA issued a report of \ntheir findings on 1 June 2019. Fairview accept the allegations and will be fined by the FCA and will have to pay \ncompensation to each customer affected. The FCA report estimates the total costs that Fairview will have to pay \nwill be in the region of £5 million.\nAudit partner comments:\nFrom discussions with the board, it is keen not to increase this provision. With the conclusion of the FCA \ninvestigation and report now published it is time to finalise figures. Whilst the amounts being considered are \nconsiderable, it will not be significant enough to affect the going concern of the business.\nICAS AA Workshop 4\n47\nNote: Materiality has been set at £2.2 million and trivial threshold at £110,000 for audit purposes\nSubsequent events\nEvent 3: Financial Conduct Authority investigation\nICAS AA Workshop 4\n48\nQ1 Evaluate the subsequent event, concluding \nwhether or not it would be an adjusting event \nQ2 Consider what, if any, additional audit \nevidence would be required\no\nWhat is the subsequent event? Did the conditions \nwhich gave rise to it occur during the year?\no\nTherefore, is this an ADJUSTING or NON-ADJUSTING \nevent?\no\nWhat is the impact to the financial statements? E.g. is a \nbalance currently over or understated?\no\nIf further audit evidence is required, write two \ntests which would help obtain this evidence\n",
