    "searchText": "Subsequent events\nEvent 4: ESG – ethical banking\nFairview has recognised that its current and potential customers are concerned with the bank’s ethical policy \non trading and its contribution to the wider community. Post year-end, the board of directors (‘the board’) \nengaged an external consultant to examine Fairview’s current ESG practices and suggest changes that it \nshould implement. This report was not available during the year-end audit but became available this week.\nFairview have added these suggestions to their sustainability report within the annual report.\nAudit partner comments:\nWe must consider the consistency of information presented in the financial statements and other sections of \nthe annual report.\nICAS AA Workshop 4\n50\nNote: Materiality has been set at £2.2 million and trivial threshold at £110,000 for audit purposes\nSubsequent events\nEvent 4: ESG – ethical banking\nICAS AA Workshop 4\n51\nQ1 Evaluate the subsequent event, concluding \nwhether or not it would be an adjusting event \nQ2 Consider what, if any, additional audit \nevidence would be required\no\nWhat is the subsequent event? Did the conditions \nwhich gave rise to it occur during the year?\no\nTherefore, is this an ADJUSTING or NON-ADJUSTING \nevent?\no\nWhat is the impact to the financial statements? E.g. is a \nbalance currently over or understated?\no\nIf further audit evidence is required, write two \ntests which would help obtain this evidence\n",
